s($,"aZm","axy",()=>{var q=null,p="images/vasco-gama-1.jpeg",o="images/gede-ruins-1.jpeg",n="images/hells-kitchen-1.jpeg",m=t.s
return A.b([A.DJ(3,B.fz,"Established in 1968 as Kenya\u2019s first marine protected area, the park is a living underwater garden of coral reefs, lagoons, coral gardens, seagrass beds, mangroves and mudflats. Its protected waters support sea turtles, rays, reef sharks, humpback dolphins and numerous reef fish.\n\nThe ocean becomes an adventure with: i) Snorkelling ii) Coral Gardens iii) Boat Excursions iv) Marine wildlife v) Swimming vi) Scuba Diving vii) Kayaking and other water sports viii) Ocean photography ix) Coastal Relaxation.\n\nKWS (Kenya Wildlife Service) places the park approximately 5km from Malindi Town via Casuarina Road.\n\n\u201cLeave the Shore behind, follow the boat into the blue, look beneath the surface and discover the Malindi most people never see.\u201d",1,q,B.bC,u.y,2000,"MALINDI MARINE NATIONAL PARK"),A.DJ(3,B.fz,"\u201cThe Stone that Remembers.\u201d Standing above the Indian Ocean, the Vasco da Gama Pillar is one of Malindi\u2019s most recognisable landmarks.\n\nIts story reaches back to 1498, when Vasco da Gama\u2019s fleet arrived off Malindi during the Portuguese voyage towards India. The National Museums of Kenya records that the Portuguese were welcomed by the Sultan of Malindi, who provided supplies and a pilot to guide the fleet across the Indian Ocean.\n\nFrom the headland, the Indian Ocean opens out in front of you, with views toward the jetty and historic harbour.\n\nExperience: i) Explore the monument ii) Ocean views iii) Photography iv) Learn Malindi\u2019s maritime history v) Sunrise/Sunset atmosphere.\n\n\u201cA monument on a cliff. An Ocean in front of you and centuries of stories beneath your feet.\u201d\n\nBest for: History lovers, photographers, couples and first-time visitors.",1,q,A.b([p,"images/vasco-gama-2.jpeg","images/vasco-gama-3.jpeg","images/vasco-gama-4.jpeg"],m),p,1500,"VASCO DA GAMA PILLAR"),A.DJ(3,B.iI,"\u201cWhere Malindi memories are kept.\u201d Before exploring Malindi\u2019s streets, it helps to understand the stories behind them.\n\nMalindi Museum presents the town\u2019s maritime history, Swahili heritage and the influence of Portuguese, British and indigenous communities. The National Museums of Kenya identifies the museum as part of a wider heritage experience.\n\nThe Malindi Heritage Complex incorporates the Vasco da Gama Pillar, Portuguese Chapel, House of Columns and the Museum itself \u2014 making it more than a building and the true starting point for understanding Malindi.",2,q,B.bC,u.Y,1500,"MALINDI MUSEUM"),A.DJ(3,B.iI,"Uncover the lost city mysteries.",3,q,A.b([o,"images/gede-ruins-2.jpeg","images/gede-ruins-3.jpeg","images/gede-ruins-4.jpeg"],m),o,3500,"GEDE RUINS"),A.DJ(3,B.m2,"Spectacular sandstone canyons.",5,q,A.b([n,"images/hells-kitchen-2.jpeg","images/hells-kitchen-3.jpeg","images/hells-kitchen-4.jpeg","images/hells-kitchen-5.jpeg","images/hells-kitchen-6.jpeg"],m),n,5000,"HELL'S KITCHEN")],A.ao("w<lH>"))})
